# Navigator global loaded-domain preview correction

## Background

Daedalus true-SPAA acceptance found a remaining RFC-0034 defect: loaded coverage has 900 observations while the active detail page has 200. The navigator selection is rendered against the 900-observation global domain, but a 40px interior drag is converted and clamped against the 200-observation active page. No local draft movement is visible within 250ms; pointer release then emits an Earlier request with `delta=-6`.

## Goal

- Use one global observation domain for navigator gesture geometry and local draft preview.
- Keep pointer movement local, frame-bounded and free of remote callbacks.
- On release, commit locally when the global draft remains inside active detail; otherwise emit one existing coverage-window intent for the drafted global start/count.
- Preserve active chart rendering, latest-wins remote sequencing, pointer capture and existing wire contracts.

## Scope / ownership

- Canonical repo: `C:\Users\Administrator\test_gemini\PulseTrade.Comm.Spa.Dynamic`
- Branch: `20260915_033.ptcs_group_support`
- Owner modules: Renderer model, WebSharper renderer, focused/browser tests, RFC/current-state docs and exact renderer client package graph.
- Do not modify TradeCore/SPAA provider logic or `G:\PulseTrade.fs\Libs\PulseTrade.Comm\doc.20261001`, which Baster owns concurrently.

## Assumptions / 假設

- Existing `ta-coverage-window.v1` can represent the drafted global ordinal/count without a wire change.
- The active detail page remains the only chart-row working set; loaded coverage is navigator authority, not a request to render every loaded observation.

## Planned steps / 計畫步驟

1. Reproduce the mixed-domain behavior in pure model and BrowserDemo tests.
2. Unify selection, pointer delta and draft in the loaded observation domain while keeping pointermove local-rAF only.
3. Verify local commit, remote typed intent, pending/resync/iframe sequencing and performance.
4. Rebuild the exact package graph, publish only after source provenance commit, perform official readback, then notify Daedalus.

## Acceptance

1. With global loaded count 900 and active detail `700+200`, an interior drag derives its delta from 900 and publishes a changed global draft by the next animation frame.
2. The preview label and navigator selection show the same global draft; chart rows and remote callback count remain unchanged during pointer movement.
3. Release inside active detail maps the global draft back to a local window and commits once.
4. Release outside active detail emits exactly one existing typed coverage intent with the drafted global ordinal/count.
5. Existing focused suites, full renderer browser/performance gates and exact package tests remain green.

## Risk / stop condition

- Converting a global draft back to local detail must reject partial/out-of-page windows rather than silently clamp to a different window.
- If the existing `TaCoverageWindowIntent` cannot represent an arbitrary drafted global window, stop before changing the public wire contract and revise RFC/Contracts explicitly.

